{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q136773926","formula":"C₁₀H₁₃NO₃","hill":"C10H13NO3","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":10.0,"H":13.0,"N":1.0,"O":3.0},"names":{"en":"2C-MMDA-3a"},"descriptions":{"en":"2C-MMDA-3a, also known as 2C-3a, MMDPEA-3a, or 2-methoxy-3,4-methylenedioxyphenethylamine (2-methoxy-MDPEA), is a psychoactive drug of the phenethylamine and MDxx families related to 3,4-methylenedioxyphenethylamine (MDPEA). It is the phenethylamine (2C) analogue of MMDA-3a and the 2-methoxy derivative of MDPEA. According to Alexander Shulgin in his 1991 book PiHKAL (Phenethylamines I Have Known and Loved), 2C-MMDA-3a has a dose range of 40 to 120 mg orally with marginal effects. At 40 mg, there was perhaps the hint of a psychic energizer (antidepressant); at 65 mg, there was pleasant mood elevation; and at 80 and 120 mg, there was brief parasthesia."},"fame":1,"pubchemCid":11127161,"mass":195.21,"charge":0,"smiles":"COC1=C(C=CC2=C1OCO2)CCN","inchikey":"AXEJSBWWIHAWJM-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2-(4-methoxy-1,3-benzodioxol-5-yl)ethanamine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"11127161","atoms":27,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":2.201,"y":1.293,"z":-0.062,"el":"O"},{"x":3.101,"y":-0.907,"z":0.332,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.585,"y":1.776,"z":-0.582,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.621,"y":-0.121,"z":0.391,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.93,"y":-0.593,"z":-0.375,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.394,"y":-0.447,"z":-0.637,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.098,"y":0.529,"z":-0.36,"el":"C"},{"x":1.245,"y":0.327,"z":-0.114,"el":"C"},{"x":1.759,"y":-0.93,"z":0.111,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.405,"y":-1.877,"z":-0.146,"el":"C"},{"x":0.959,"y":-2.054,"z":0.102,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.191,"y":-0.237,"z":0.657,"el":"C"},{"x":3.375,"y":0.504,"z":0.221,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.417,"y":2.737,"z":0.462,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.574,"y":0.382,"z":-1.333,"el":"H"},{"x